Creating your API endpoint
1. Open your hosting file folder (public_html, or htdocs,  or www depends on the hosting)
2. Create a folder with name using your group number e.g. group1
3. Upload the files to your folder.
4. Open config.php and update the credentials coming from your own database settings.
5. Open phpmyadmin and create the table as reflected in the schema.sql
6. To test your setup, open www.postman.com, in the url bar, use GET method, and the url to your API endpoint e.g. site.sample.com/group1
7. Click Send and expect a list of items from your table. 
